This is the READ.ME file for the (unregistered) version of Telix 3.22
posted for BBS distribution. Telix 3.22 as posted for BBS distribution
consists of the following four ZIP archives:

        TLX322-1.ZIP    Executable and support files.

        TLX322-2.ZIP    MODEMCFG.EXE (modem configuration program),
                        CS.EXE and CSS.EXE (script compilers), QDHost
                        Mode script source files, and dialing directory
                        conversion program. Also TELIX322.NEW,
                        describing new features in v3.22.
        
        TLX322-3.ZIP    Host+ Bulletin Board for Telix (formerly Host 5.0)

        TLX322-4.ZIP    SALT.DOC, the SALT script language ref. manual.
                        TELIX.DOC, the Telix program reference manual
                        SIMPLE.DOC, the SIMPLE script language ref. manual
                        HOSTPLUS.DOC, the Host+ BBS program manual

Note that these ZIP files are encoded with an Authenticity Verification
number. If you use PKZIP 1.10 or later to extract from thse archives,
PKZIP should display the symbol -AV beside each filename, and should
finish with the following message:

  Authentic files Verified!   # MUP129   deltaComm Development

Note that while the Telix documentation has been re-formatted and
cleaned up to some extent, the contents have not changed significantly
since v3.10. All additions are described in TELIX322.NEW, so if you
printed out the manual(s) for v3.10 to 3.21 you do not have to do so
again for this release (other than the HostPlus.DOC and SIMPLE.DOC, new
to version 3.20).

