The file TELIX322.NEW describes new features in this version of Telix.

To start off you should make a copy of all the files, for safe-keeping.
Hard disk users should create a TELIX directory and copy all the files
into it. Floppy disk (360k) users should put the contenets of the first
archive onto one disk, and optionally put the script compiler (CS.EXE)
from the second archive onto that disk as well. That might leave things
a bit cramped though. If there is a space problem, keep in mind that
script source files (*.SLT) and the script compiler do not have to stay
on your main Telix disk.  With these files on another disk, there should
be plenty of space.

The best way to continue is by printing out the documentation which can
be done by using the DOS copy command (at the DOS prompt) to copy the
file(s) to the printer, as follows:

     copy TELIX.DOC prn
     copy SALT.DOC prn
     copy SIMPLE.DOC prn
     copy HOSTPLUS.DOC prn

Once the manual has finished printing, see the section called 'Getting 
Started'.

Please see LICENSE.DOC for complete ordering/upgrade information.

The Telix documentation is formatted to use 66 lines/page, as supported
by most printers. Many laser printers print only 60 lines/page by
default. Running the LASER66.COM program included will set up an HP
Laserjet or compatible laser printer to print 66 lines/page, and will
also allow it to print IBM lindrawing characters, which are used in the
documentation.

